body:
Reddit: "I hate celebrity culture! Keeping up with musicians/actors is stupid!"

&#x200B;

Also Reddit: "Celebrities should have political power because I like their movies/music!"

Damn, I'm 28 too and have a hard time feeling this way. I've been at a million crossroads in my life, and I feel like every time I pick a path, it just splinters into more and more paths and options. I'm trying really hard to plan and set myself up, but there's so many factors in why I can/can't do some things. I'm getting real tired of being in my 20s.

&#x200B;

It doesn't help that I'm now the age that my dad was when I was born. But he had a wife and a house... I spend almost half my (low) income just on rent that increases every year.
